==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|last|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|lästʹlē}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈlɑːstli/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lastly.wav|Audio (southern England)}}
* {{a|GA}} {{enPR|lăstʹlē}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈlæstli/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːstli|q1=Received Pronunciation|æstli|q2=General American|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|last|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|sequence}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to mark the beginning of the last in a list of items or propositions.}}
#: {{ux|en|Firstly, that's illegal; secondly, it has serious disadvantages; thirdly, it's not necessary; and '''lastly''', did I mention that it's illegal?}}
# {{lb|en|discourse marker}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to signal that the speaker is about to yield control of the conversation}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|last in order}} {{l|en|finally}}, {{l|en|last}}, {{l|en|last of all}}; see also [[Thesaurus:lastly]]
